# EEVS Multi-License Notice

This repository uses a split licensing model:

1. **Core Server Engine (`src/`) — GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0)**
   - All source files inside [`src/`](./src) are licensed under the **GNU General Public License v3.0** (see [`src/LICENSE`](./src/LICENSE)).
   - Any modified versions, forks, or binary distributions of the core `eevs` server must remain open-source under GPL-3.0.
   - **Plugin Linking Exception**: Under Section 7 of the GNU General Public License v3.0, the copyright holders grant you additional permission to compile, link, and load shared-library plugins (`.dll` / `.so`) that communicate with `eevs` exclusively through the public C++ Plugin SDK headers in [`include/eevs/`](./include/eevs) under any license of your choice (open-source or proprietary), without requiring those plugins to be licensed under the GPL.

2. **SDK, Example Plugins, Scripts & Demo (`include/`, `plugins/`, `scripts/`, `demo/`, `tests/`) — MIT License**
   - The public C++ Plugin SDK headers ([`include/`](./include)), example plugins ([`plugins/`](./plugins)), FiveM Server SDK resource ([`scripts/`](./scripts)), showcase resource ([`demo/`](./demo)), and test suite ([`tests/`](./tests)) are licensed under the **MIT License** (see [`LICENSE.MIT`](./LICENSE.MIT)).
   - Third-party developers are free to use, modify, and distribute plugins and FiveM resources built with these components under any terms.
